# TypeScript SDK — Workflows and tasks - Hatchet
created: 2026-03-25, last updated: 2026-04-12, [Read more](https://mintlify.wiki/hatchet-dev/hatchet/sdk/typescript/workflows-tasks)

Durable tasks survive worker restarts and support long-running waits backed by Hatchet’s durable event log.
Create them with `hatchet.durableTask()` or `workflow.durableTask()`.
...
export const waitForApproval = hatchet.durableTask({
name: 'wait-for-approval',
executionTimeout: '24h',
fn: async (input: { orderId: string }, ctx) => {
// Pause until the 'order:approved' event arrives for this order
const event = await ctx.waitForEvent(
'order:approved',
`input.orderId == "${input.orderId}"`
);
return { approved: true, event };
},
});
```
Durable tasks can also be added to a workflow using `workflow.durableTask()`:
```
const wf = hatchet.workflow({ name: 'approval-flow' });
wf.durableTask({
name: 'await-approval',
executionTimeout: '24h',
fn: async (input, ctx) => {
await ctx.sleepFor('5m');
const event = await ctx.waitForEvent('order:approved');
return { event };
},
});
